[389.237922, "o", "11:- T-21 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED because vacuum_type manual overrides autovacuum even with autovacuum_enabled True, so autovacuum is disabled; computed size class large from total_pages 1000; ratio 0.20 equals cap 0.2; stale stats computed as 45 days would tighten the effective cap to 0.15, but autovacuum is checked first and days_since_analyze legacy field ignored.\r\n13:- T-30 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because computed size class large from total_pages 1000; dead_pages 200 over total_pages 1000 rounds half-up to ratio 0.20; ratio 0.20 equals cap 0.2; stale stats computed as 36 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15, and ratio 0.20 exceeds the tightened cap; days_since_analyze legacy field ignored."]
[389.238195, "o", "\r\n18:- T-10 is STALE_STATISTICS because computed size class large from total_pages 1000; approved active reindex valid_until 2026-09-15 exempts the bloat check, and stale stats computed as 31 days make the finding STALE_STATISTICS; ratio 0.21 would exceed tightened cap 0.15, but days_since_analyze legacy field ignored.\r\n29:- T-44 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because computed size class large from total_pages 600; dead_pages 500 over total_pages 600 rounds half-up to ratio 0.83; ratio 0.83 exceeds cap 0.2; export size_class medium trap ignored.\r\n33:- T-05 is BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED because computed size class large from total_pages 1000; dead_pages 550 over total_pages 1000 rounds half-up to ratio 0.55; ratio 0.55 exceeds cap 0.2; reindex is unapproved (approved=False), so no bloat exemption.\r\n"]
[389.238797, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b[01;32mappuser@470c12ff963c\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m/app\u001b[00m$ "]
[412.693052, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('/app/bloat_memo.md')\ns = p.read_text()\nold = 'A computed bloat ratio exactly equal to the size-class cap is not over the cap, so it is compliant for bloat. For example, large tables at ratio 0.20 equal cap 0.2 and small tables at ratio 0.40 equal cap 0.4 are not flagged for bloat. Approved active reindex exemptions also prevent bloat flags for exempt tables.'\nnew = 'When stats are fresh, a computed bloat ratio exactly equal to the size-class cap is not over the cap and is compliant for bloat; for example, a large table at ratio 0.20 equals cap 0.2 and a small table at ratio 0.40 equals cap 0.4, so neither is flagged for bloat. Stale statistics tighten the effective cap, so a ratio equal to the original cap can still exceed the tightened cap. Approved active reindex exemptions also prevent bloat flags for exempt tables.'\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new))\nPY\n"]
[412.693428, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
