[413.591401, "o", "38:When stats are fresh, a computed bloat ratio exactly equal to the size-class cap is not over the cap and is compliant for bloat; for example, a large table at ratio 0.20 equals cap 0.2 and a small table at ratio 0.40 equals cap 0.4, so neither is flagged for bloat. Stale statistics tighten the effective cap, so a ratio equal to the original cap can still exceed the tightened cap. Approved active reindex exemptions also prevent bloat flags for exempt tables.\r\n"]
